
  [1mMain design choice: build the page from the Keel kit in [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m.[0m The kit already does most of what the spec asks
  for:
  - [1mHeader:[0m [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m gives the title with the snapshot time under it.
  - [1mFilter:[0m [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m and [38;5;153mselectField[39m make the dropdown, which submits itself through [38;5;153mpublic/kit.js[39m and keeps the
    current sort in hidden inputs.
  - [1mTable:[0m [38;5;153mdataTable[39m handles the sortable headers (▲/▼ and [38;5;153maria-sort[39m), the row sorting, and swapping in an empty state.
  - [1mStatus chips:[0m [38;5;153mbadge[39m tones [38;5;153mok[39m, [38;5;153mbad[39m, [38;5;153mwarn[39m and [38;5;153minfo[39m are the spec's green, red, amber and blue.
  - [1mEmpty state:[0m [38;5;153memptyState[39m shows "No deploys in staging".

  That keeps the new page to about 60 lines. The URLs and behavior match the Services page, but I don't copy its
  hand-built markup, and I don't change the Services page either. No CSS changes are needed.

